<start_working_out>
Let's assume the total number of blocks that Henrikh has to walk to work is 'x'. 
The time taken to walk to work is x * 1 minute = x minutes. 
The time taken to ride his bicycle to work is x * 20 seconds = x * (20 / 60) minutes = x/3 minutes. 

Since it takes him 8 minutes more to walk than to ride his bicycle, we can set up an equation:

x * 1 minute = x/3 minute + 8 minutes


